src/vendor/nanoarrow/ is the output of upstream's ci/scripts/bundle.py
run on the archive with --symbol-namespace=zuarrow --with-ipc
--with-flatcc, without the C++ .hpp wrappers, plus LICENSE.txt and
NOTICE.txt, with exactly the patches above applied. One layout change:
the bundler pastes ipc/flatcc_generated.h into nanoarrow_ipc.c, and
here it is kept as nanoarrow_ipc_flatcc_generated.h and included, so
clang does not warn about its unused static inline functions. The
upstream lines are unchanged and in the bundler's order. tools/derive-vendor
is the derivation and tools/verify-vendor re-runs it and fails on any
difference.

Patches:
  0001-no-suppressing-pragmas.patch  removes the '#pragma GCC/clang
      diagnostic ignored' lines from flatcc's pdiagnostic.h, because R
      CMD check reports pragmas that suppress diagnostics.
  0002-unused-locals.patch  drops an unused local from one generated
      FlatBuffers macro and marks an assert-only local as read, so -Wall
      reports no unused variable without the pragmas 0001 removes.
  0003-dictionary-compression.patch  gives a DictionaryBatch's decoder the
      body's codec and the caller's decompressor, so a compressed
      dictionary is decompressed rather than read as raw bytes. To be
      offered upstream (pedrobtz/zuarrow#17).
  0004-ipc-views-and-ree.patch  lets the IPC reader decode the
      binary-view, string-view, list-view, large-list-view and
      run-end-encoded layouts (design D17; nanoarrow #833, #824): their
      schema types, and the variadic data buffers RecordBatch.
      variadicBufferCounts names for each view node. To be offered
      upstream.
  0005-footer-magic-read.patch  formats a bad file trailer as the six
      bytes compared; upstream prints a %s from one past the end of the
      unterminated input, a heap over-read the fuzz target found.
  0006-header-size-overflow.patch  rejects a message length that would
      overflow the int32_t header size with its prefix, signed overflow
      UBSan found under the fuzz target.
  0007-dictionary-index-type.patch  reads a dictionary encoding with no
      indexType as int32, as Schema.fbs says, instead of dereferencing
      the absent table (a NULL read the fuzz target found).
  0008-absent-tables.patch  rejects a message, footer or field whose
      union names a table it does not carry, which the decoder would
      otherwise read through a NULL pointer (found by the fuzz target).
  0009-dictionary-batch-counts.patch  checks a DictionaryBatch's field
      node and buffer counts against the dictionary's schema, as a
      record batch's are; without it the walk read past the node vector
      (found by the fuzz target).
  0010-metadata-strings.patch  reads metadata keys and values by their
      stored length, absent ones as empty: strlen() cut binary values at
      a NUL and read a NULL key (found by the fuzz target).
  0011-list-view-sizes.patch  makes minimal validation size a list
      view's sizes buffer, which it skipped, so full validation read an
      unchecked buffer (found by the fuzz target).
  0012-offsets-buffer-size.patch  makes default validation read offsets
      only from a buffer that holds them: a zero-length array with a
      short offsets buffer was read past its end (found by the fuzz
      target).

